# Board selection for the knob project — the mirror of
# components/board/Kconfig.projbuild's choice (the shared board component
# is not added to this build, so the choice lives in the knob's board
# shim; the root Kconfig.projbuild is not processed by ESP-IDF 5.5).
# All three options stay spelled exactly like the clock's choice: the
# shared components' Kconfig lines (moon MOON_ALBEDO_W "default 2048 if
# BOARD_P4", the ui Kconfig's per-board defaults) reference the symbols,
# and Kconfig errors on undefined symbols in `if` clauses. This project
# defaults to BOARD_KNOB; S3/P4 stay selectable-but-unused so a stray
# shared-Kconfig `if` still parses.
choice BOARD
    prompt "Board"
    default BOARD_KNOB

config BOARD_KNOB
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-Knob-Touch-LCD-1.8 (360x360) [this project]"
    help
        The knob: 360x360 SH8601 QSPI round LCD, CST816S touch, EC1 dial
        (no push-button), LEDC backlight, battery ADC on GPIO1, NO IMU,
        NO RTC IC, NO audio codec. Real esp_deep_sleep_start; the time
        base is the internal RTC timer + SNTP (software path, as on the
        P4). Third board of the moon-clock family.

config BOARD_S3
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75 (466x466) [clock project]"

config BOARD_P4
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-XC (720x720) [clock project]"
endchoice
